version numbering schema:
M.N.P
| | +-- patch: increased if only bug fixed were incorporated
| +---- minor: increased if syntax/semantic breaking changes were applied
+------ major: increased if elementary changes (from user's point of view) were made

2.0.0 (2026-10-18)
 - added: Markdown Viewer (Ctrl+Alt+M, toolbar) with a live preview of the active document
 - added: viewer docked as side panel or detached to a maximizable window (Detach/Dock button)
 - added: viewer option to follow the caret and mark the selected blocks (Follow caret)
 - added: viewer engines Microsoft Edge WebView2 (default if available) and RichEdit (fallback)
 - added: WebView2 used via WebView2Loader.dll next to NppToolBox.dll or the installed runtime
 - added: viewer engine EdgeHTML of the legacy Microsoft Edge (Engine=2)
 - added: links in the viewer opened in the browser, Notepad++ or the default application
 - added: target of the hovered link shown in a bar below the viewer
 - added: copy from the viewer with Ctrl+C and the context menu
 - added: viewer in GitHub's dark style in Notepad++'s dark mode
 - added: settings section [Viewer] (Engine, FollowCaret, Detached, UpdateDelay)
 - added: settings section [Toolbar] to show or hide each toolbar icon
 - changed: Rust 1.95 or newer required to build
 - changed: windows-core added as runtime dependency (COM interfaces of WebView2)
 - changed: toolbar icons rendered at runtime in the exact size of the toolbar and DPI
 - changed: resvg added as runtime dependency (SVG icon rendering)
 - fixed: alert icons missing in Copy as HTML (LibreOffice, Office) and in the RichEdit viewer
 - fixed: pictures in the RichEdit viewer drawn over the paragraph above and cut off at the bottom
 - fixed: Rewrap joining the alert marker line (> [!NOTE]) with the alert text
 - fixed: image embedding test using an invalid file: URI on Windows

1.0.0 (2026-10-16)
 - first release
